# ── OPERATOR FLAGS (r108) — runtime state in a TRACKED source directory ─────
# data/ holds real modules (candle_feed.py), so these are ignored by NAME and
# not by directory. Both are set ONLY by devtools (67 and 68) and read live by
# the running services; neither is ever committed.
# ⚠️ FEED_MAINTENANCE has worked untracked since 2026-08-15 by luck rather than
# intent — nothing on a box runs `git add`. Written down now so a future
# `git add -A` on a control-side checkout cannot capture an operator flag and
# ship someone else's maintenance window to the fleet.
data/FEED_MAINTENANCE
data/REHEARSAL_OFF
# 🔴 r68 — THREE MORE SENTINELS THAT WERE NEVER LISTED, AND THE COMMENT ABOVE
# PREDICTED EXACTLY THIS. `NO_MIDNIGHT_HALT` (r21) and `DRILL_DISK` have been
# untracked by the same luck since they were introduced, and r67 added
# `SHUTDOWN_CAUSE` as a third — found because it showed up in `git status`
# right after that bake. `AGENT_STATUS` is r68's own and is listed with them
# rather than becoming a fourth instance of the same gap.
data/NO_MIDNIGHT_HALT
data/DRILL_DISK
# r171 (AGT.1/AGT.2) - the agent watcher's event record and its observe-only
# trading verdicts. Runtime records, never committed; never purged.
data/AGENT_EVENTS.jsonl
data/AGENT_VERDICTS.jsonl
data/SHUTDOWN_CAUSE
data/CAP_PAGED
data/CAP_PAGED.tmp
data/AGENT_STATUS
env/
ohlc/
orb_range.json
orb_state.json
reports/
trades.db
trades.db-shm
trades.db-wal
venv/

